# PRTERM Configuration Reference

Complete configuration reference for **PRTERM 1.0.0**.
Users copy needed sections into `prterm.ini`; missing keys use compiled-in defaults.

## Sections

### `[site]` — Station identity & UI language

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `name` | `PRTERM` | Station name (header bar) |
| `subtitle` | *(empty)* | Subtitle; empty = hidden |
| `language` | `en` | UI language: `en\|de\|es\|pt\|fr` |

### `[station]` — Global station defaults (inherited by `[station:NAME]`)

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `callerid` | `PRTERM-1` | Callsign (6 chars + optional -N SSID) |
| `qth` | *(empty)* | Location name (e.g. "MGH") |
| `locator` | *(empty)* | Maidenhead grid (e.g. "JN49VL") |

### `[ui]` — Web interface

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `font_file` | *(empty)* | .otf/.ttf path; empty = system mono |
| `font_size` | `14` | CSS pixels (6-96) |
| `line_height` | `1.2` | Multiplier (1.0-2.0) |
| `density` | `compact` | `compact` \| `normal` |
| `rows` | `0` | Terminal rows; 0 = auto |
| `columns` | `0` | Terminal columns; 0 = auto |
| `theme` | `silver` | `silver` \| `dark` |

### `[radio]` — Global defaults only

Device-specific settings (driver, port, baud, modem, line, kiss_init, freq_hz, mode) belong in `[station:NAME]` sections. These global keys are kept as fallback for backward compatibility.

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `duplex` | `half` | `full` \| `half` (RX during TX?) |
| `tx_power_mw` | `4000` | TX power mW (0-12000) — compliance limit |
| `rx_poll_ms` | `250` | RX poll interval ms (50-10000) |
| `max_log` | `500` | Max log lines in UI (20-20000) |

Legacy fallback keys (prefer `[station:NAME]` instead):

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `driver` | `sim` | `sim` \| `tnc2` \| `tmodem` |
| `port` | `/dev/ttyUSB0` | Serial device to TNC |
| `baud` | `115200` | Serial baud rate (300-4000000) |
| `radio_baud` | `1200` | Channel baud: TNC2C=2400, PK-TNC2=1200 |
| `modem` | *(empty)* | Modem type (e.g. "tcm3105") |
| `line` | `8n1` | `8n1\|7e1\|7o1\|8e1\|8o1` |
| `kiss_init` | `esc` | KISS entry: `esc\|auto\|tapr` |
| `freq_hz` | `27125000` | Frequency in Hz |
| `mode` | `am` | `fm\|am\|ssb\|lsb\|usb\|cw` |

### `[admin]` — Web administration

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `enabled` | `true` | Admin area enabled? |
| `user` | `admin` | Admin username |
| `pass_hash` | *(empty)* | SHA256 hash; empty = built-in default "PRTerm" |
| `session_ttl_min` | `480` | Session timeout minutes (1-10080) |
| `allow_guest_tx` | `true` | Guest users may transmit? |

### `[mailboxd]` — MailboxD BBS integration

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `enabled` | `false` | Show MailboxD tab and link? |
| `dir` | `/var/mailboxd` | Install dir; socket at `<dir>/prterm.sock` |

### `[daemon]` — TNC daemon (prterm-tncd)

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `resend_kiss_params` | `false` | Re-send KISS CSMA params after repair? |

### `[debug]` — Logging

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `level` | `warn` | `off\|error\|warn\|info\|debug\|trace` |

### `[callsign]` — Callsign validation rules

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `callid_max_len` | `6` | Max base-call length (1-10) |
| `callerid_base_len` | `6` | CallerID base length (1-10) |
| `callerid_max_total` | `8` | Total length incl. SSID (1-16) |
| `callerid_allow_ssid` | `true` | Allow "-N" suffix? |
| `callerid_ssid_digits` | `1` | SSID digits after '-' (0-2) |

### `[ban]` — Banned callsigns

Wildcard patterns (`*` = any, `?` = single char) mapping to reasons.

### `[paths]` — Runtime directories

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `runtime_dir` | `./prterm.runtime` | Session/state dir (relative to CGI binary) |

### `[station:NAME]` — Per-station TNC/rig configuration

Each `[station:NAME]` defines one complete station: own TNC, own radio, own antenna. All device-specific settings live here.

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|-------|
| `driver` | `tnc2` | `sim` \| `tnc2` \| `tmodem` |
| `port` | `/dev/ttyUSB0` | Serial device (use stable by-id path) |
| `baud` | `19200` | Serial baud rate to TNC |
| `radio_baud` | `1200` | On-air data rate (HARDWARE, not changeable) |
| `modem` | *(empty)* | Modem type (e.g. "tcm3105") |
| `line` | `8n1` | `8n1\|7e1\|7o1\|8e1\|8o1` |
| `kiss_init` | `esc` | KISS entry: `esc` (TNC2C), `auto` (PK-TNC2), `tapr` (TAPR), `native` (BayCom/PTY, T-Modem) |
| `mode` | *(empty)* | `fm\|am\|ssb`; empty = inherit `[radio]` mode |
| `freq_hz` | `0` | Frequency in Hz; 0 = inherit `[radio]` freq_hz |
| `callerid` | *(inherits)* | Station callsign (inherits `[station]` if empty) |
| `antenne` | *(empty)* | Antenna description (display only) |
| `enabled` | `true` | Station active? |

**KISS init modes:**
- `esc` — `ESC @K` without `\r` (Landolt TNC2C, TheFirmware)
- `auto` — `ESC @K`, repeated when firmware only echoes "kiss on" (PK-TNC2, TheFirmware class)
- `tapr` — `"kiss on\r"` (real TAPR devices only)
- `native` — device already speaks KISS from power-up: the daemon opens the port and writes nothing. Used for the BayCom PTY and the T-Modem-c1224 / s1224 (received frames arrive without FCS there — the firmware strips the trailer itself).